{"schemaVersion": 1, "id": "9baff81e-a651-44d3-b477-4176d4bd8e61", "timestamp": "2026-11-07T22:25:00Z", "runtime": "executorch-xnnpack", "engineVersion": "v1.5.1", "engineArtifact": "llama_main sha256:61e7e881a4e3e12d38e3d102e01e15119b33395c164229fa21ab351b6a174e0e", "model": {"id": "own-export/Qwen3-1.7B-ET1.5.1-xnnpack-8da4w-emb8-ctx2048", "quantization": "8da4w: int8 dynamic per-token asymmetric activations x int4 symmetric weights, group 128, HQQ scale-only (every Linear incl. lm_head); embedding int8 per-row (embedding_byte); fp32 compute and KV cache; own export, ExecuTorch 1.5.1", "sha256": "76b68b2c2735f3808aff9f13bde07043fda24aad2be774aa1ff3d2ea750b553d", "file": "Qwen3-1.7B-ET1.5.1-xnnpack-8da4w-emb8-ctx2048.pte", "hfRevision": "70d244cc86ccca08cf5af4e1e306ecf908b1ad5e"}, "task": "long-context-1024-gen256", "device": {"systemName": "macOS", "modelIdentifier": "Mac16,9", "chip": "Apple M4 Max", "systemVersion": "Version 27.0 (Build 26A428)", "processorCount": 16, "physicalMemoryMB": 131072, "batteryState": "unknown", "buildConfiguration": "Release"}, "conditions": {"executorchRunner": "llama_main", "sampler": "greedy (--temperature 0: argmax)", "maxOutputTokens": 256, "chatMode": "host chat template: HF apply_chat_template(add_generation_prompt=True), template defaults (transformers 5.0.0rc1, Qwen/Qwen3-1.7B@70d244cc86cc); llama_main --prompt_file, num_bos 0", "thinkingPolicy": "model default: the chat template rendered without enable_thinking (Qwen 3: thinking on); reasoning tokens count against the same budget", "cpuThreadsPolicy": "engine heuristic (--cpu_threads -1: cpuinfo get_num_performant_cores)", "contextSource": "recipe.json export.max_context_length", "contextBudget": 2048, "contextTokens": 2048, "warm": false, "regime": "cold", "thermalInitial": "nominal", "thermalFinal": "nominal", "loadAverage": 6.794921875, "loadAverages": [6.794921875, 8.75537109375, 11.06787109375], "busyOthers": ["dasd:99%", "launchd:28%", "Google Chrome Helper (Aperitif Renderer):27%"], "cpuSpeedLimit": null, "exitCode": 0, "launchWallSeconds": 18.211, "runIndex": 1, "textCheck": {"status": "PASS", "alphanumericCount": 965, "distinctWords": 101, "taskTerms": true, "flags": [], "method": "the runner's generated text (parsers: textExtraction) + lexical screen; full text retained"}, "textOutputSHA256": "76ad0c027ef88cc0e342f6a622f3026f94c158b276fd04ac31113eb8ebb51792", "promptVersion": "noref-2026-10-19"}, "metrics": {"promptTokenCount": 1355, "generatedTokenCount": 255, "promptTokensPerSecond": 887.9423328964613, "decodeTokensPerSecond": 50.73617190608834, "firstTokenLatencyMS": 1526, "loadTimeSeconds": 7.5, "coldRun": true, "harnessStamp": "executorch-mac-v1-2026-10-08", "initialThermalState": "nominal", "finalThermalState": "nominal", "memoryPeakResidentMB": 2044.921875}, "harnessStamp": "executorch-mac-v1-2026-10-08", "decodedText": "<think>\nOkay, let's tackle this query. The user wants me to list 25 distinct things that on-device AI allows a phone to do that a cloud model can't. And each item needs two full sentences of explanation, numbered, and no stopping early.\n\nFirst, I need to recall what on-device AI is. It's processing done on the device's hardware, not relying on the cloud. So, the phone can process data locally, which is different from cloud-based models that require internet and server processing.\n\nNow, thinking about the differences. Cloud models are off-device, so they can't process data locally. On-device AI can handle tasks like image recognition, voice recognition, or even some form of machine learning, but they can't do things that require local processing without the device.\n\nSo, for each of the 25 points, I need to make sure they are distinct and not overlapping. Let me brainstorm some points.\n\n1. Local data processing: On-device AI can process data locally, so it doesn't need internet or cloud. That's a key difference.\n\n2. Real-time processing: Since the device can process data locally, it can handle tasks that require real-time processing, like voice recognition or image recognition.\n\n3. Reduced latency: Because", "outputSample": "<think>\nOkay, let's tackle this query. The user wants me to list 25 distinct things that on-device AI allows a phone to do that a cloud model can't. And each item needs two full sentences of explanati", "provenance": {"definitions": "prefill tok/s = prompt_tokens / (prompt_eval_end_ms - inference_start_ms) * 1000. The window opens before the runner tokenizes the prompt (TextLLMRunner::generate sets inference_start_ms, then encodes), so prefill includes tokenization.\nTTFT ms = first_token_ms - inference_start_ms = the same window (first_token_ms is taken when prefill returns, before the first token is decoded to text).\ndecode tok/s = generated_tokens / (inference_end_ms - prompt_eval_end_ms) * 1000, generated_tokens = tokens of the decode loop; the reply has one more token, the one prefill sampled.\ncold = one generation in a fresh llama_main process (no --warmup). warm = llama_main --warmup: one unmeasured generation of the same prompt and max_new_tokens in the same process, stats and KV position reset, the second generation measured.\nClock: integer milliseconds (extension/llm/runner/util.h time_in_ms).", "recipe": "Qwen3-1.7B-ET1.5.1-xnnpack-8da4w-emb8-ctx2048.recipe.json", "recipeSha256": "f311a97dcc67800520311ea0a305bbc053301ead88cb77c0d1342b3c4c7250e0", "recipeAlias": "et1.5.1-xnnpack-8da4w-g128-emb8", "exporter": "extension/llm/export/export_llm (examples/models/qwen3/config/qwen3_xnnpack_q8da4w.yaml)", "modelProvenance": "own export with the ExecuTorch tag's own exporter (recipe.json beside the .pte); not a published artifact", "promptFile": "Qwen3-1.7B-ET1.5.1-xnnpack-8da4w-emb8-ctx2048.prompts/long-context-1024-gen256.chat.txt", "promptSha256": "e8cfb3f021c4ce7c00b3ea24d91950ad3f5dd8f64dceb58a5058be68539b0fd9", "tokenizer": "tokenizer.json", "tokenizerSha256": "aeb13307a71acd8fe81861d94ad54ab689df773318809eed3cbe794b449